- ❌ Do NOT keep `buildContextEntries()` as the source — it is compaction-aware and DIVERGES from the filter's getBranch source, breaking the S4 inverse-map coherence. Switch to getBranch().slice().reverse().
- ❌ Do NOT forget `.slice().reverse()` — getBranch() returns LEAF→ROOT; the filter passes ROOT→LEAF. Forgetting the reverse makes indexToEntryId back-to-front.
- ❌ Do NOT build indexToEntryId in a separate loop from messages — they MUST be pushed together (same loop, same order) so indexToEntryId[i] aligns with messages[i] exactly.
- ❌ Do NOT set `hideEntryIds: []` on the payload — OMIT it when empty (conditional spread → undefined) so the persisted JSON is clean and S4's 'absent → live fallback' path is exercised.
- ❌ Do NOT let capture failure escape — resolvePreview is already wrapped by rewindExecute step 5's try/catch; just add `hideEntryIds: []` to the fallback. NEVER add a second try/catch that could swallow the wrong thing.
- ❌ Do NOT edit markers.ts (S1 shipped the field + spread) or transforms.ts (S2 shipped the helper) or filter.ts (S4's territory).
- ❌ Do NOT filter compaction ids out of hideEntryIds — sessionEntryToContextMessages(compaction) yields 1 message so its id can land in hideEntryIds; S4's mapEntryIdsToMessageIndices stops at compaction and won't resolve it (harmless live fallback). Only the `.filter(string+non-empty)` guard is needed.
- ❌ Do NOT rely on `vitest run` alone for type correctness — expectTypeOf is a runtime no-op; ALWAYS also run `npx tsc --noEmit`.
